      "sample_index": 4,
      "text": "The force required to loosen a bolt varies inversely with the length of the handle of the wrench used. This means that the product of the force and the length of the handle is a constant. We can set up the equation as follows:\n\nForce × Length = Constant\n\nGiven that a wrench with a handle length of 9 inches requires 375 pounds of force, we can find the constant:\n\n375 × 9 = 3375\n\nNow, we want to find the force required for a wrench with a handle length of 15 inches. We can use the same constant and set up the equation:\n\nForce × 15 = 3375\n\nTo find the force, we divide both sides of the equation by 15:\n\nForce = 3375 / 15\nForce = 225\n\nTherefore, a wrench with a handle length of 15 inches will require 225 pounds of force to loosen the same bolt.",
