      "sample_index": 5,
      "text": "To solve this problem, we need to use the concept of inverse variation. In an inverse variation, the product of two quantities is constant. Here, the force \\( F \\) and the length of the handle \\( L \\) are inversely proportional, so we can write:\n\n\\[ F \\times L = k \\]\n\nwhere \\( k \\) is a constant.\n\nFirst, we need to find the constant \\( k \\). We know that a wrench with a handle length of 9 inches requires 375 pounds of force. So, we can substitute these values into the equation:\n\n\\[ 375 \\times 9 = k \\]\n\nCalculating the right-hand side, we get:\n\n\\[ k = 3375 \\]\n\nNow that we have the constant \\( k \\), we can use it to find the force required for a wrench with a handle length of 15 inches. We substitute \\( L = 15 \\) and \\( k = 3375 \\) into the equation:\n\n\\[ F \\times 15 = 3375 \\]\n\nTo find \\( F \\), we solve for \\( F \\) by dividing both sides of the equation by 15:\n\n\\[ F = \\frac{3375}{15} \\]\n\nCalculating the right-hand side, we get:\n\n\\[ F = 225 \\]\n\nTherefore, the force required to loosen the bolt with a wrench of 15 inches is \\(\\boxed{225}\\) pounds.",
